   "html": "<p>### Byte Quest registration hardening (quick review 19:56, reproducibility auditor, Codex)</p><ul><li><strong>The E12–E16 predictions are bound to exact configs:</strong> the sha256 of all 30 staged byte configs was appended to <code>experiments/checks/PREDICTIONS.md</code> (\"Config binding…\"), still before any byte run. Any change needs a new dated entry.</li><li>The EOS 0x00 collision check was already in the builder.</li><li><strong>SQ221:</strong> byte-dataset rebuild determinism (before the first byte run).</li></ul><p>### Vast.ai CLI (the human's request: install it on Windows and hook it to the cockpit)</p><ul><li><code>vastai</code> 1.11.2 is installed for the Windows user Python (ARM64) at <code>%APPDATA%/Python/Python312-arm64/Scripts/vastai.exe</code> (not on PATH; the cockpit will call it by full path). It's also installed in the WSL cockpit venv.</li><li><strong>Windows ARM64 workaround:</strong> vastai pins <code>cryptography==49.0.0</code>, <code>pillow==12.2.0</code> and <code>pycares==4.11.0</code>, which have no ARM64 wheels, so it was installed with <code>--no-deps</code> plus binary-only dependencies (cryptography 46.0.3, pillow 13.0.0, pycares 5.2.1). <strong>Tested:</strong> <code>--version</code>; <code>show instances</code> authenticates (0 instances); <code>search offers</code> returns 37 verified RTX 3090 offers, cheapest $0.113/hr.</li><li><strong>The API key is NOT in the repo</strong> (checked with <code>git grep</code> and a tree scan). It lives in the human's <code>Desktop/shared/api keys.md</code> (added as <code>VAST_API_KEY</code> in its env block, at the human's request) and in vastai's own config (<code>~/.config/vastai/vast_api_key</code>, Windows).</li><li><strong>No instance was rented.</strong> Renting spends money and needs the human's explicit go-ahead per rental (AGENTS §0a); the SQ220 pilot is still parked.</li></ul>"
