   "version": "v0.4.41",
   "title": "Research: image and audio inputs (nice-to-have, research only)",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong> (human: \"research subagent about supporting audio and image inputs, ... nice to have for later, keep it research only\"): two Sonnet research subagents, no code, no downloads, no GPU.</p><ul><li><strong><code>notes/research-image-input.md</code></strong>: 6 approaches compared (frozen encoder + projector, patch-as-tokens, discrete image tokens, cross-attention adapters, early fusion; tiny VLMs; Mamba/linear-time VLMs; ternary vision encoders; looped multimodal). <strong>Recommendation (medium confidence)</strong>: a narrow synthetic proof of concept, a tiny 1-3M-param conv/patch stem feeding 32-64 prefix tokens, trained on self-rendered matplotlib/turtle images paired with their Python source (no licence issues); fallback: Flamingo-style gated cross-attention from the coda. Key constraints: image tokens inside the looped core cost r times (keep them &lt;= 64); a bidirectional 2D encoder feeding the causal core (VL-Mamba/Cobra pattern); ternary vision exists (ViT-1.58b, BitVLA, TernaryCLIP) with the first layer kept high-precision; the smallest published VLM LM is ~135M (10x ours). Several arXiv ids are marked unverified.</li><li><strong><code>notes/research-audio-input.md</code></strong>: <strong>recommendation (medium confidence, ~60%)</strong>: discrete semantic audio tokens at 12.5-25 Hz added to the vocab (~2k rows; Mimi codebook-0, GLM-4-Voice tokenizer or HuBERT units), interleaved audio/text training: no LM change, fits GDN's streaming state; T=1024 = ~82 s of audio at 12.5 Hz. Fallback: frozen Moonshine-/Whisper-tiny encoder + projector (as big as our LM). Evidence for GDN on ASR is thin (no LibriSpeech GDN result found); Speech Slytherin finds Mamba's ASR advantage minor; no ternary from-scratch audio model found. Cheapest PoC described (LibriSpeech-100 with codec tokens, shuffled-audio control). Licences flagged (EnCodec weights CC-BY-NC; Mimi licence conflicting between sources).</li><li><strong>Status</strong>: both are post-v1.0.0 arcs, after the K9 cleanup and the core thesis. Paper lists (~60 ids, some flagged unverified) will be checked before being added to <code>refs/fetch_refs.py</code>.</li></ul>"
