   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong> (the human, about <code>experiments/checks/results/</code> and worktrees: why isn't this in the repo?):</p><ul><li><strong>Audit:</strong></li><li>The repo has exactly one checkout and no worktrees (<code>git worktree list</code>: only <code>C:/Users/mreca/Desktop/Gogeta-0 [main]</code>).</li><li>All 8 check results (K1–K6, K7-parity, sq_06) are tracked and on GitHub.</li><li><strong>The gap was the training runs:</strong> 15 run folders (<code>meta.json</code>, <code>summary.json</code>, <code>samples.txt</code>) existed only on the WSL disk under <code>~/fusiondance-data/runs/</code>. That includes E0/E1/E2's records and the K7 sweep runs, so the devlog's training numbers had no committed source file.</li><li>The old <code>C:\\Users\\mreca\\Desktop\\FusionDance</code> folder is a stale v0.1.1 copy; it has no results.</li><li><strong>Fix:</strong> <code>experiments/runs/sync.sh</code> mirrors each finished run's record files into <code>experiments/runs/&lt;run&gt;/</code> (a few KB each; refuses token-like strings; never checkpoints or data). This version commits 11 runs: E0 s0, E1 s0 (v0.3.0), E2 s0, a smoke run, and the 7 K7 sweep runs finished so far. The 4 without a <code>summary.json</code> are skipped: E9 s0 and E2 s1 were killed before finishing, one smoke run, and the K7 run still in flight.</li><li><strong>Root cause:</strong> the generic <code>runs/</code> rule in <code>.gitignore</code> (from v0.1.0, meant for training output folders) also matched <code>experiments/runs/</code>, so run records could never be committed. <code>.gitignore</code> now re-includes <code>/experiments/runs/</code>.</li><li><strong>AGENTS §5:</strong></li><li>every result lives in the repo; run <code>sync.sh</code> before each version, and only checkpoints, data, caches and raw logs stay outside git;</li><li>one checkout, no worktrees, for subagents too;</li><li>never read from or write to the stale FusionDance copy.</li></ul>"
