   "version": "v0.4.13",
   "title": "K7 and K8 registered: LR sweep and external reference",
   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong>: registers the two checks that the Phase 2 campaign runs first and last. Predictions and decision rules are committed here, <strong>before any run</strong>.</p><ul><li><code>experiments/checks/k7_lr_sweep.py</code> (applies the K7 rule and writes the next campaign; rule logic tested on 8 synthetic cases), <code>experiments/launch/campaigns/phase2a-k7-lr.campaign</code> (8 short runs) and <code>phase2b-replication.template</code>.</li><li><code>experiments/checks/k8_external_reference.py</code>: doc-level bits/char for our checkpoints and SmolLM2-135M. It loads only from the local cache, at the pinned revision <code>93efa2f</code>, and refuses on a mismatch.</li><li><code>experiments/checks/PREDICTIONS.md</code>: K7, K8, and the <strong>replication protocol</strong> with its comparison criteria. Cards K7 and K8.</li><li>AGENTS.md: campaign runner and <code>--lr</code> (§5); controls are LR-tuned before use and E10 becomes the control (§6); docs table rows.</li><li>Site regenerated (<code>docs/</code>) and <code>experiments/INDEX.md</code> regenerated from committed sources; version 0.4.13.</li></ul><p>### K7: LR tuning for E10 (control) and E1 (best hybrid)</p><ul><li><strong>Question:</strong> what's each model's best peak LR? Every earlier run used an untuned 3e-3.</li><li><strong>Result:</strong> not run. Phase 2a: lr ∈ {1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 6e-3} × {E10, E1}, seed 0, 20M tokens, ~43 min GPU.</li><li><strong>Verdict vs prediction:</strong></li><li>Prediction: E10's best is 3e-3 or 6e-3, E1's is 2e-3 or 3e-3, both curves flat near the optimum, and 1e-3 is 3–8% worse.</li><li>Rule: the lowest full-val loss wins (ties go to the smaller LR). If the winner is at the grid edge, extend one step (at most twice per side).</li><li><strong>What it means:</strong> the replication (E10 / E1 / E11 × 3 seeds, E9, conditional E0 and E2) then runs at the tuned LRs.</li><li><strong>Card:</strong> experiments/cards/K7.md</li></ul><p>### K8: External sanity reference (SmolLM2-135M, bits/char)</p><ul><li><strong>Question:</strong> are our loss numbers in a sane range against a well-known public model?</li><li><strong>Result:</strong> not run (runs after Phase 2b, ~5 min).</li><li><strong>Verdict vs prediction:</strong></li><li>Prediction: SmolLM2 0.28–0.45 bits/char, ours 0.21–0.26.</li><li>K8a: ours ≥ 0.5 × SmolLM2, else suspect train/val leakage.</li><li>K8b: doc-level bits/char within 5% of the training-time value.</li><li><strong>What it means:</strong> a sanity ceiling only (10× larger, different data, possible contamination), not a control.</li><li><strong>Card:</strong> experiments/cards/K8.md</li></ul><p><strong>Phase 2 GPU budget</strong> (estimated from v0.3.0 wall times): ~6.5 h if both tuned LRs are 3e-3, up to ~8.5 h with conditional runs and grid extensions.</p>"
