   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong>: check K2 (BitLinear speed vs nn.Linear): script, results JSON and card. Prediction committed in <code>f1b4ebd</code> before it ran.</p><p>### K2: BitLinear speed vs nn.Linear</p><ul><li><strong>Question:</strong> Does ternary make compute cheaper in our code? (C14)</li><li><strong>Result:</strong> BitLinear forward is <strong>5.58× / 4.06× slower</strong> (384→1024 / 384→2048); fwd+bwd 1.92× / 1.59× (<code>results/K2.json</code>).</li><li><strong>Verdict vs prediction:</strong> Hit on direction; the slowdown slightly exceeds the predicted 1.5–5×. C14 confirmed WRONG FOR OUR CODE.</li><li><strong>What it means:</strong> Ternary is a memory win only until we have real ternary kernels; never claim speed from it.</li><li><strong>Card:</strong> experiments/cards/K2.md</li></ul>"
